<title>HONG KONG: Manila's Singson sees no sharp peso devaluation.</title>
<headline>Manila's Singson sees no sharp peso devaluation.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philippines Central Bank Governor Gabriel Singson said on Thursday in Hong Kong that he saw no sharp devaluation of the peso.  </p>
<p>&quot;Devaluation won't work. A sharp devaluation of the currency won't solve our problem,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;Our exchange rate policy is to let the market decide the exchange rate and we intend to continue. My statement is unqualified.&quot;</p>
<p>The peso fell prey to Asian currency turmoil last week following a speculative attack on the Thai baht.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6352</p>
